A1. The kind of people who solve all of the Judge puzzles. ~ COMPETENT
A9. Where Greta Garbo gets her' background. ~ STUDIO
A11. What the flighty globe trotters expect to do. ~ AVIATE
A14. We have tried to make this superlatively clear. ~ PUREST
A15. Left the seashore for an ocean voyage. ~ EBBED
A16. Some people will do this to the finish just as soon as they get a new car. ~ MAR
A17. As cold weather approaches this is going to be felt but not so much as last year (plur.). ~ HATS
A20. Last winter these started on the downward path. ~ SLEDS
A22. All that was left after the grasshopper finished. ~ ORT
A23. One of the large colleges that is not in the football league. ~ VASSAR
A25. Look at this in the mirror and notice the marks of time. ~ EMIT
A26. It is plain to be seen that the world is all wrapped up in this. ~ CELLOPHANE
A28. It won't be long now when you can do this to that radio announcer. ~ SEE
A29. Mother always whips this for dressing in the kitchen. ~ CREAM
A30. These have caused many tears. ~ RENTS
A33. Tan makes this look like the devil. ~ SA
A34. The kind of cracks that cause sides to split. ~ WISE
A37. To defeat utterly. ~ ROUT
A38. Thus it is and thus it will be. ~ SO
A40. Most anyone with a taking manner can do this. ~ STEAL
A42. These sometimes go with bounds. ~ METES
A45. In Chicago these have been having troubles of their own. ~ INS
A47. A soft shelled nut. ~ PSYCHOPATH
A50. No mother wishes to have these get in ahead of her children at school. ~ NITS
A52. What the neighbors consider mother's little darling. ~ TERROR
A53. A dead letter. ~ PHI
A54. A prognostic saying. ~ SOOTH
A56. What Old Sol will do when he pats you on the back. ~ SEAR
A57. Babies used to cry for it. ~ PAP
A58. Air routes. ~ NARES
A60. Horsed around. ~ DRIVEN
A63. When one does this it is bad form but it is good form that makes one do it. ~ STARES
A65. What we should like to do to the one who took the spare tire. ~ LOCATE
A66. Back in the gay nineties these were often seen hanging around the stage doors. ~ PORTIERES

D1. Completed in detail. (We will not vouch for its pedigree.) ~ CUR
D2. It sounds as if someone was indebted for this poetical idea. ~ ODE
D3. When you meet this one you are just out of luck. ~ MISHAP
D4. They found this in the ashes. ~ POTASH
D5. You can fit this to almost any tune. ~ TA
D6. This one was just a side issue. ~ EVE
D7. A fellow who has an exaggerated opinion of himself. (His always comes first.) ~ NIBS
D8. Many personal contacts are made under this. ~ TABLE
D9. To be this is a woman's secret ambition. ~ SPARER
D10. This is often seen on the highway carrying his house with him. ~ TURTLE
D12. What Detroit does with the unemployed. ~ TEEMS
D13. When these circle the seashore it is one of the current events of the season. ~ EDDIES
D16. Indian dog kennels. ~ MOCCASINS
D18. This was old Nick himself. ~ TSAR
D19. We are giving you some thing more sensible this time. ~ SANER
D21. This brought Marlene Dietrich to stardom. ~ STEAMSHIP
D23. The outcome of this will bring relief to the farmer. ~ VOMIT
D24. Many people in this place are planning to leave the United States. ~ RENO
D27. An overproduction of these in the country has also caused hardships. ~ LAWS
D31. A bunch of trouble. ~ TUMOR
D32. What every military man wishes to get into. ~ STEP
D35. When you get this far in the month there is only an ember of summer left. ~ SEPT
D36. What a moratorium does to a financial strain. ~ EASES
D39. These are always stewing about something. ~ ONIONS
D41. Some Greek picked this for a song. ~ LYRE
D43. Just a little piece of machinery. ~ TAPPET
D44. The constituent of illuminating gas that causes the blue flame. ~ ETHANE
D46. This one is lucky enough to have an ermine coat. ~ STOAT
D48. Where Dad earned his first rocks. ~ CRADLE
D49. This is enough to give you the willies. ~ HORROR
D51. When this is on a soft shoulder it is apt to skid. ~ STRAP
D55. The man who goes shopping with his wife. ~ HERO
D59. What a chicken might weigh in India. ~ SER
